  "limits": [
    "Five owned 64 MiB snapshot virtio fixtures and one boot-image disk; actual UFS root on 14.5 and ZFS root on 15.1. Physical/controller/multi-host/mirror or RAIDZ label qualification remains separate.",
    "Existing random unmounted single-leaf pool on HVM-UNIQUE-4K is exported without force. Its independently recorded GUID is reimported with -N -d on that exact owned disk without force, then guarded cleanup removes only that pool. These are disposable test-only writes; product code performs no native I/O or mutation.",
    "Active/exported labels retain independently observed pool identity and recorded state; exported pool disappears from imported catalogue while its label facts remain positive. Actual export invalidates combined review. Wrong-address/unavailable controls alter only capture copies. Reimport preserves original independently observed catalogue identity/backing and active label state.",
    "Whole closed exported fixture bytes remain unchanged across read-only zdb/fstyp/diskinfo/hash observations and comparisons. Previous foreign/root/system/signature checks rerun; all original host backings/base/runtime are preserved, owned disks/image/key/variables removed and process groups stopped.",
    "The qualified positive grammar is version 5000, native member states 0/1/2 and bounded scalar/container metadata. Quoted strings with embedded apostrophes or colon-plus-space delimiters refuse; destroyed-state positive handling has portable coverage only.",
    "Default zdb -l groups identical configurations and reports checksum only for the representative label. Four-index group coverage is not all-label checksum verification or integrity, complete pool topology/membership, all signature absence or safe reuse. Positive destroyed state has portable coverage only.",
    "Unsupported/error/partial captures refuse with no observation. Capture syntax cannot prove successful execution, freshness, completeness, provenance or atomicity. Unknown outputs never establish blank/unused/eligible state.",
    "No runtime collector/helper/HTTP/CLI wiring, complete device-use clearance, raw-open/locality/shared-host fencing, enrollment/reservations/durable jobs or product mutation authority. Complete slice 1 and later M2 acceptance gates remain open.",
    "Final PR-head portable review is separate; subsequent documentation/evidence updates must leave all recorded functional/test/tool input hashes unchanged."
  ]
